<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Texcoco</h1><p class="st-meta">1337 CE – 1521 CE (approx.) · capital Texcoco</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Acolhua capital on the eastern shore of Lake Texcoco, a partner in the Aztec Triple Alliance and famed as a centre of law, poetry and learning.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Texcoco became the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acolhua">Acolhua</a>, a Chichimec-descended people of the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-mexico">Valley of Mexico</a>, in the 14th century. In 1418 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tepanec-empire">Tepanec Empire</a> killed its ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ixtlilxochitl-i">Ixtlilxochitl I</a> and occupied it, forcing his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nezahualcoyotl">Nezahualcoyotl</a> into exile.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nezahualcoyotl">Nezahualcoyotl</a> regained Texcoco in 1428-31 and made it a co-leader of the Aztec <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Triple Alliance</a>. He built palaces, gardens and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texcotzinco">Texcotzinco</a> hill retreat, organised legal councils, and was celebrated as a poet-king. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nezahualpilli">Nezahualpilli</a> was famed as a judge and astrologer. Texcoco ruled many towns of the eastern valley.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> interference in Texcoco's succession after 1515 divided it, and one faction under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ixtlilxochitl-ii">Ixtlilxochitl II</a> aided Cortés, who built his brigantines there in 1521. Its last independent king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cacamatzin">Cacamatzin</a> died in Spanish custody in 1520.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1337 CE – 1521 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><pat